114-| `spawn.preferred_agentic_system` | Currently effective `{mode, allowed_providers, source, config_key}`, or `null`. During an active schedule window, `source` is `schedule`. |
115-| `spawn.schedule` | `{configured, timezone, config_key, windows, active_window, base_preferred_agentic_system}`. `timezone` is always `UTC`; every projected window also carries its normalized bounds, key, and provider-system projection. |
116-| `spawn.launch_composition` | `{enabled, config_key, contract, schema_version, degradation}` without invoking `agents-infra`. |
117-| `spawn.ceilings` | `{contract_version, configured, config_path, codex, claude, qwen}`; each provider reports `configured` and only its configured model/criterion/effort/role fields. |
118-| `spawn.selection` | Required flags plus provider effort vocabularies and supported model criteria. |
119-| `spawn.execution` / `spawn.tracking` | Executable background mode and durable run-observation contract. |
120-| `goals` | Static compact `board-goal-v2` capability with required Session Manager native reflection and the one-release `primary-goal-v1` / `board-goal-v1` adapters. The legacy `goals.primary` descriptor remains nested alongside the v2 fields for the compatibility release. It never embeds the current objective and is omitted from `view=spawn-preflight`. |
121-| `version_control` | `{configured, confirm, desired_commit_time, enforced_types, owner_message, acknowledgement_parameter, acknowledgement_value, config_key}`. |
122-
123-Local mode uses `spawn.*` keys. Remote mode uses `remote.spawn.*` when that
124-object is present and non-null; otherwise it falls back to the whole root
125-`spawn` object. The reported `spawn.config_key_prefix` and nested `config_key`
126-values always identify the effective source. `preferred_agentic_system` is the
127-canonical config spelling; `preferred_agent_system` is not an alias.
