159-## DSL Mutations — structured writes for agents
160-
161-Write operations through the same DSL engine. All mutations support `--dry-run` preview. Destructive mutations require `--confirm`.
162-
163-```bash
164-# Status changes
165-task-board m 'set_status(TASK-12, status=development)'
166-
167-# Evidence-backed role handoff (preferred producer end transition)
168-task-board handoff TASK-12 --role developer
169-
170-# Task/Bug estimate enum
171-task-board m 'set_estimate(TASK-12, estimate=notEstimated)'
172-task-board m 'set_estimate(TASK-12, estimate=estimated, scale=fibonacci, number=5)'
173-
174-# Create elements
175-task-board m 'create(type=task, parent=STORY-05, name=new-task)'
176-task-board m 'create(type=task, parent=STORY-05, name=new-task, description="Implement feature", scope="Backend only", ac="Tests pass")'
177-
178-# Update README fields
179-task-board m 'set_details(TASK-12, title="New title", description="Updated desc")'
180-
181-# Rename overview name/slug while preserving ID, README, progress, children, and resources
182-task-board m 'rename(TASK-12, name=better-task-name)'
183-
184-# Assignment
185-task-board m 'assign(TASK-12, agent=claude-opus)'
186-task-board m 'unassign(TASK-12)'
187-
188-# Dependencies
189-task-board m 'link(TASK-13, blocked_by=TASK-12)'
190-task-board m 'unlink(TASK-13, blocked_by=TASK-12)'
--
205-task-board m 'add_resource(TASK-12, name="TASK-12_design.md", type=precondition, content="...", description="Design doc")'
206-task-board m 'update_resource(TASK-12, name="TASK-12_design.md", type=precondition, content="revised", description="Design doc v2")'
207-task-board m --confirm 'delete_resource(TASK-12, name="TASK-12_design.md")'
208-
209-# Destructive — preview first, then confirm
210-task-board m --dry-run 'delete(TASK-12)'
211-task-board m --confirm 'delete(TASK-12)'
212-
213-# Batch mutations (semicolon-separated)
214-task-board m 'set_status(TASK-12, status=done); set_status(TASK-13, status=development)'
215-```
216-
217-**Safety flags:**
218-- `--dry-run` — preview mutation without applying. Returns what would change
219-- `--confirm` — required for destructive mutations (`delete`, `delete_resource`)
220-- Mutation arguments are schema-checked. Unknown named arguments and extra positional fragments are rejected with typed errors before any write runs.
221-- Without `--confirm`, destructive mutations are rejected with an error
222-
223-**Format:** `--format json` (default) or `--format compact`
224-
225:**Introspection:** Run `task-board q 'schema(mutation=NAME)'` for one mutation signature, or full `schema()` for the entire contract.
226-
227-`task-board handoff` resolves the role's configured end status, verifies all
228-checklist items plus an actual stored task-scoped outcome, and serializes that
229-decision with the ordinary status transition. The underlying shared `handoff`
230-mutation carries the already-resolved role/status for remote execution; use the
231-CLI facade so callers do not have to reproduce role-policy resolution.
232-
233-The `estimate` q field is a nested enum. Task/Bug values are either
234-`{"kind":"notEstimated"}` or
235-`{"kind":"estimated","scale":{"kind":"fibonacci","number":5}}`.
236-Story/Epic values are calculated, never persisted or hand-set. Full coverage
237-returns the same `estimated` shape with the descendant sum. Partial coverage
238-returns
239-`{"kind":"partiallyEstimated","rolledEstimate":{"kind":"estimated","scale":{"kind":"fibonacci","number":5}},"notEstimatedCount":"1/3","unestimatedTaskIds":["TASK-..."]}`.
240-Story counts direct Task/Bug children; Epic rolls up descendant Task/Bug values.
241-New Task/Bug records must be estimated before entering `development`; legacy
242-records with no persisted Estimate section remain compatible and count as
243-unestimated in container projections.
