263-## CLI — human-facing output and complex operations
264-
265-CLI text output with ANSI colors is designed for humans. Use for operations not covered by DSL, or when human-readable output is needed.
266-
267-When reporting board state to a person, reference each epic, story, task, or bug with both its concrete ID and its human-readable title/name. In practice, that usually means carrying both `id` and `name` in your query output, or using a preset such as `default` or `overview` that already includes them. ID-only references are not enough for chat summaries because readers should not have to resolve identifiers manually.
268-
269-```bash
270-# Good human-facing summary inputs
271:task-board q --format compact 'list(type=task, status=development) { id name status }'
272:task-board q --format compact 'list(type=story, parent=EPIC-260218-abc123) { overview }'
273-```
274-
275-### Parent alignment in the unified goal ledger
276-
277-Use the top-level `goal` group to maintain one provider-neutral, board-scoped
278-statement of the current `parent/primary` owner's complete objective. It
279-survives a parent-session replacement, records immutable `board-goal-v2`
280-revisions, and never changes a board element's status or acceptance evidence.
281-The command group is the one-release `primary-goal-v1` compatibility adapter.
282-
283-```bash
284-# Create only when no primary goal is active.
285-task-board goal set-primary \
286-  --objective "Keep the parent goal aligned with the current user requirements." \
287-  --reason "First actionable requirement"
288-
289-# CAS-replace the whole objective. Repeating the same objective is idempotent.
290-task-board goal update --if-revision 1 \
291-  --objective "Keep the parent goal aligned with the current user requirements and active delivery work." \
292-  --reason "Requirement expanded"
293-
294-# Read current state, immutable audit history, or one immutable revision.
295-task-board goal get
296-task-board goal get --history
297-task-board goal get --goal-id PRIMARY-GOAL-260723-a1b2c3 --revision 1
298-
299-# Clear only with the observed revision and an explicit disposition reason.
300-task-board goal clear --if-revision 2 --reason "Parent intent superseded"
301-```
302-
303-`goal get` is read-only and remains available inside a spawned run. When
304-`TASK_BOARD_RUN_ID` is set, `set-primary`, `update`, and `clear` return the
305-typed `primary_goal_parent_context_required` failure with no side effects;
306-spawned owners must use `task-board spawn goal` or `task-board spawn goal
307-upsert` for their `run/RUN-*` owner. Both commands use `board-goal-v2`; owner
308-isolation prevents either compatibility adapter from silently updating or
309-clearing the other.
310-
311-Every successful JSON response has `ok`, `board_scope`, `primary_goal`, and
312-`latest_ref`; mutations additionally carry `mutation`. Exact revision reads
313-add `primary_goal_revision`, and history reads add newest-first `history`
314-summaries. Typed failures use
315-`{ok:false,error:{code,message,current_ref,side_effects:false,remediation?}}`.
316-Remote primary-adapter mutations accept authoritative `goal=board-v2` or the
317-one-release `primary_goal=board-v1` compatibility capability. Direct v2
318-mutations require `goal=board-v2`, and reads never create a local shadow
319-ledger.
