314-**Auto-detection:** Codex runtimes expose `CODEX_SESSION` or `CODEX_THREAD_ID` (and sometimes `CODEX_CI` in managed environments). If any of these are present, affinity is Codex; otherwise it is Claude. These hints are agent-affinity signals only: they do not discover an endpoint, authenticate a thread, create an addressable caller goal plane, or select Qwen. Canonical exclusive/mixed policy and active schedule windows constrain affinity before use. Auto-detection never chooses a model or reasoning effort. Use an in-set `--agent` to make provider selection explicit.
