333-## Close the Review Loop
334-
335-The Orchestrator owns producer -> reviewer -> rework -> reviewer cycles until accepted `done`:
336-
337-1. A producer's `to-review` handoff triggers an explicitly selected reviewer child immediately.
338-2. Accepted work reaches `done` from the reviewer verdict.
339-3. Requested changes become preserved rework context for the appropriate producer through `to-dev` or `analysis`.
340-4. Revised work goes through a new reviewer. Repeat until accepted.
341-5. A child that exits before handoff or leaves the item parked in `analysis`, `development`, `testing`, or `reviewing` is inspected, retried, or rerouted through a focused child; recoverable work is never handed to the human.
342-6. A genuine `blocked` verdict stops the loop only for an evidence-backed external blocker or unresolved human-only platform/product/architecture/tradeoff/approval decision, with the full evidence packet and exact human decision or external input needed to resume.
343-
344-Requested changes, failed tests, recoverable child exits, and retryable runtime failures are not a reason to stop or ask the human to review. Before genuine escalation, persist the constraint, evidence, failed assumptions/attempts, viable alternatives and tradeoffs, recommendation, and exact human decision or external input needed to resume.
345-
346-## Preflight And Audit Hygiene
347-
348-Spawn-contract reviews get noisy if you search the whole repo without filtering transient runtime copies.
349-
350-- Use target-only `project_config(view=spawn-preflight, role=ROLE, agent=PROVIDER?)` for an actual spawn decision. Use full `project_config()` only when auditing local/remote runtime configuration.
351-- Exclude `.temp/**` from repo-wide grep/review by default. This repo contains historical task-scoped worktrees such as `.temp/*/skill-project-management-worktree/` that can preserve pre-refactor spawn files and create false drift.
352-- Prefer searching canonical source paths directly: `README.md`, `SKILL.md`, `references/`, `.specs/`, and `tools/board-cli/`.
353-- If you need runtime artifacts, inspect the specific run directory under `.temp/spawn-runs/RUN-.../` instead of grepping all of `.temp/`.
354-
355-Recommended search pattern:
356-
357-```bash
358-rg -n "spawn|project_config|--background|task-path|dod-path" \
359-  README.md SKILL.md references .specs tools/board-cli \
360-  -g '!**/.temp/**'
361-```
362-
363-**What spawn does:**
364-1. Validates element on board
365-2. Loads role config from `.roles/<name>/role.md` (required)
366-3. Loads task metadata from the board (README fields, checklist, parent, resources)
367-4. Verifies the task brief is usable (description + AC)
368-5. Verifies task-specific DoD exists on the board
369-6. Composes prompt from role template plus board state
370-7. Resolves and validates the selected provider's project MCP launch composition, or records a bare-launch degradation
371-8. Assigns to agent (name includes archetype: `[implementer] developer (codex)`)
372-9. Adds any missing role baseline DoD items to the board checklist without duplicating already injected items
373-10. Saves prompt to `.temp/prompts/{YYMMDD}-{HH-mm-ss}_{agent-name}_{task-id}.md`
374-11. Creates `.temp/spawn-runs/RUN-.../{manifest,state,runner.log}`
375-12. Queues a tracked background runner and returns a `RUN-...` handle immediately
376-13. The runner claims a slot under `spawn.max_parallel`, launches the agent process, streams logwork, and runs the completion hook
377-14. Logs queue/start/completion and sanitized launch-composition details to element notes
