643-
644-## Template-Based Prompt Composition
645-
646-Spawn always composes the prompt from the role template:
647-
648-1. Reads task README (title, description, scope, acceptance criteria)
649-2. Reads precondition resources from progress.md
650-3. Loads each resource's content from `.task-board/.resources/`
651-4. Renders everything through a Go template
652-
653-The resolved `agent_context.profile` selects one of two embedded templates:
654-
655-- `full` is the backward-compatible default. It renders the historical role
656-  body, CLI reference, run-control, saving, safety, completion, and workdir
657-  sections unchanged.
658-- `lite` renders a compact invariant/command role contract. It keeps the exact
659-  FIRST/LAST lifecycle commands, merged task+role DoD, lazy skill catalog, task
660-  metadata/preconditions, task-scoped outcome command, literal `to-review`
661-  handoff wording, reviewer verdict branches, compact Stop-The-Line evidence
662-  packet, and workdir. Selection, checklist injection, completion-hook evidence
663-  enforcement, run tracking, and reviewer routing remain board/runtime gates
664-  outside the presentation template.
665-
666-Because a lite worker receives one concrete element and its task inputs, its
667-prompt uses compact task-specific projections and skips routine `summary()`,
668-`plan()`, `schema()`, and `{ full }`. Scoped schema remains available after an
669-unknown call; broad routing and audit reads remain Orchestrator/full-profile
670-tools.
671-
672-The **full default template** is embedded in the binary and includes:
673-- Task metadata (ID, title, description, scope, AC, parent)
674-- Precondition resource contents as "Instructions" sections
675-- Board CLI reference (status updates, checklist, notes, resource saving)
676-- Explicit instructions to save results via `task-board m 'add_resource(..., type=outcome)'` on first write and `update_resource(...)` for revisions
677-- Task-scoped artifact naming guidance such as `TASK-260218-abc123_results.md`
678-- Logbook guidance for important findings, decisions, anomalies, or regressions
679-- Completion-hook contract: if a spawned task lands in `to-review` without a new task-scoped outcome artifact, the hook leaves a blocking note and reverts the task to its start status
680-
681-**Project-local template overrides** are profile-specific:
682-
683-- `.agents/spawn-template.md` for `full`
684-- `.agents/spawn-template-lite.md` for `lite`
685-
686-Both expose the same data:
687-```
688-{{.TaskID}}                    — element ID
689-{{.TaskTitle}}                 — from README title
690-{{.TaskDescription}}           — from README description
691-{{.TaskScope}}                 — from README scope
692-{{.TaskAC}}                    — from README acceptance criteria
693-{{.ParentID}}                  — parent element ID
694-{{.AgentName}}                 — agent display name (e.g. "[implementer] developer (claude)")
695-{{.BoardDir}}                  — path to .task-board/
696-{{.PreconditionResources}}     — slice of {Name, Description, Content}
697-{{.RoleName}}                  — role name (e.g. "developer") — empty if no --role
698-{{.RoleDescription}}           — compact description from role.md frontmatter
699-{{.RoleBody}}                  — markdown body from role.md
700-{{.Archetype}}                 — "implementer", "analyst", "reviewer", "tester"
701-{{.Skills}}                    — slice of {Name, Path} — resolved lazy skill catalog refs
702-{{.StartStatus}}               — status to set on launch (e.g. "development")
703-{{.EndStatus}}                 — status to set on completion (e.g. "to-review")
704-{{.DoDContent}}                — merged DoD: task-specific board checklist + role baseline DoD
705-```
706-
707-**Workflow for spawning:**
708-```bash
709-# 1. Put task-specific DoD on the board
710-task-board m 'add_checklist_item(TASK-260218-abc, text="OAuth2 flow works end-to-end")'
711-task-board m 'add_checklist_item(TASK-260218-abc, text="Token refresh handles edge cases")'
712-task-board m 'add_checklist_item(TASK-260218-abc, text="Rate limiting returns 429")'
713-
714-# 2. Link precondition resources (optional — provides additional context)
715-task-board m 'add_resource(TASK-260218-abc, name=TASK-260218-abc_impl-guide.md, type=precondition, content="...", description="Implementation guide")'
716-
717-# 3. Spawn with explicit role/model/reasoning selection
718-task-board spawn TASK-260218-abc --role developer --background --agent codex --model gpt-5.6-sol --reasoning-effort max
719-
720-# 4. Agent runs, saves results
721-# (agent runs: task-board m 'add_resource(TASK-260218-abc, name=TASK-260218-abc_results.md, type=outcome, content="...", description="Implementation notes")')
722-```
