942-## Choosing Agent Type
943-
944-Board task work must go through tracked spawn with explicit role/model selection;
945-Codex and Qwen also need an explicit compatible effort. Runtime-native helper
946-agents can still exist for non-board exploratory chat when the human explicitly
947-requests inline execution, but they are not an execution path for tracked board tasks.
948-
949-| Factor | `spawn --agent claude` | `spawn --agent codex` | `spawn --agent qwen` | Native helper agents / Task tool |
950-|--------|----------------------|---------------------|--------------------|-------------------------------|
951-| Board integration | Automatic (spawn) | Automatic (spawn) | Automatic (ordinary tracked runs) | Not allowed for board task execution |
952-| Role support | `--role` flag (auto status, DoD, skills) | Same | Same | No board role lifecycle |
953-| Model validation | Explicit model; reasoning rejected | Explicit model + compatible effort | Explicit model + compatible effort | N/A |
954:| Goal-bound owner | Supported | Supported | Not supported | No board goal lifecycle |
955-| Prompt persistence | Auto-saved to `.temp/` | Auto-saved to `.temp/` | Auto-saved to `.temp/` | In conversation context only |
956-| Model discovery | `models(agent=claude)` | `models(agent=codex)` | `models(agent=qwen)` | Runtime-specific |
957-| Billing metadata | Provider API | OpenAI API / ChatGPT | Qwen Token Plan Team metadata in registry | Runtime-dependent |
958-
959-**Recommendations:**
960-- Resolve `preferred_agentic_system` and the active schedule window first. With no canonical restriction, Claude/Codex runtime affinity remains the fallback; select Qwen explicitly or through canonical/scheduled policy.
961-- Use Codex when you want OpenAI model diversity or Codex-specific behavior. Query the current registry; the July 2026 lineup runs from `gpt-5.6-sol`/`terra`/`luna` through `gpt-5.5`, `gpt-5.4`, `gpt-5.4-mini`, and `gpt-5.3-codex-spark`, each with an explicit compatible effort.
962-- Use Qwen only with a registered Qwen model and explicit supported effort; ordinary child tracking is supported, but a `--goal-scope` owner must use Codex or Claude.
963-- Do not use native helper agents / Task tool for board task work. If it belongs on the board, it needs a tracked `RUN-...` handle from a fully explicit spawn.
964-- For research-heavy board tasks, prefer `task-board spawn TASK-... --agent claude --model claude-opus-5 --role researcher --background` when Claude's context is the deliberate choice.
965-
