968-## Real-World Example: What Went Wrong
969-
970-**Project:** MTS Tariff Research, Phase 1 — 6 parallel research stories.
971-
972-**Attempt 1:** `codex exec -m codex-5.3` — Model not supported with ChatGPT account. All 6 agents died instantly. Empty logs.
973-
974-**Attempt 2:** `codex exec -m gpt-5.2` — Model works, agents start, update task-board, read methodology files, do web searches. But all 6 run out of context before writing output files. Zero deliverables.
975-
976-**Historical note:** Phase 0 used Claude Code Task tool with opus model — 3 parallel agents, each produced 500-700 line research documents in ~6 minutes. That was useful before tracked background spawn was the board contract, but it is no longer the recommended board execution path.
977-
978-**Lesson:** For research-heavy board tasks (web search + read docs + synthesize + write large output), prefer tracked `spawn --agent claude --model claude-opus-5 --role researcher --background` over untracked native helpers or context-limited Codex runs.
