1024-
1025-## Permissions, Trust, and Unsafe Modes
1026-
1027-### Why Codex spawn uses unsafe mode
1028-
1029-Tracked background spawn launches real child agent processes, and those children may themselves spawn tracked background children. A Codex child running inside Codex's `workspace-write`/seatbelt sandbox cannot reliably launch another Codex process: nested runs can fail during app-server/PATH-alias initialization with `Operation not permitted`.
1030-
1031-For that reason `task-board spawn --agent codex` uses:
1032-
1033-- `--dangerously-bypass-approvals-and-sandbox` for non-interactive approvals and no sandbox
1034-- `--skip-git-repo-check` when needed for non-standard temporary workspaces
1035-
1036-Implication: spawned Codex agents execute with the same machine-level trust assumptions as Claude spawn (`--dangerously-skip-permissions`). Only use this workflow in trusted repos on trusted machines.
1037-
1038-### Trust configuration (repo-level)
1039-
1040-Mark project as trusted in `~/.codex/config.toml`:
1041-
1042-```toml
1043-[projects."/absolute/path/to/repo"]
1044-trust_level = "trusted"
1045-```
1046-
1047-This removes trusted-directory checks for that repo.
1048-
1049-### `--skip-git-repo-check` vs full trust
1050-
1051-`--skip-git-repo-check` bypasses only git/trust validation for a run. It does **not** disable sandbox restrictions.
1052-
1053-Use when:
1054-- quick one-off test in a non-standard directory
1055-- you do not want to persist trust config
1056-
1057-### Manual full-access mode
1058-
1059-For unrestricted execution (no sandbox, no approval stops):
1060-
1061-```bash
1062-codex exec \
1063-  -m gpt-5.6-sol \
1064-  -c 'model_reasoning_effort="max"' \
1065-  --dangerously-bypass-approvals-and-sandbox \
1066-  -C /absolute/path/to/repo \
1067-  - < .temp/prompts/agent.md
1068-```
1069-
1070-Use only on trusted repos/machines.
1071-
1072-### Safety checklist before unsafe mode
1073-
1074-1. Confirm working directory is correct (`pwd`, `-C` path).
1075-2. Ensure prompt has no destructive commands (`rm -rf`, broad `git reset`, etc.).
1076-3. Limit scope to one task and one repo.
1077-4. Log output to file for auditability.
1078-5. Prefer explicit tracked spawn (`--role`, `--background`, `--model`, and Codex/Qwen `--reasoning-effort` when applicable); use manual launch only as a fallback.
1079-
1080-### Permission/trust error map
1081-
1082-- `Not inside a trusted directory and --skip-git-repo-check was not specified`
1083-  - Fix: add repo to `~/.codex/config.toml` trust list or run with `--skip-git-repo-check`.
1084-
1085-- `SandboxDenied` / operation not permitted for filesystem or process commands
1086-  - Fix: keep work in workspace, or rerun with unsafe mode if strictly needed.
1087-
1088-- Stream disconnects to `chatgpt.com/backend-api/codex/responses` in restricted environments
1089-  - Fix: rerun outside restrictive sandbox/network path; verify account/model availability.

