`build_toolchain_untested_release`, although both gates would reject it;
33. `go.mod` `go` directive above resolved; 34. `go.mod` `toolchain` directive
above resolved; 35. `rust-toolchain.toml` `channel = "nightly"`;
36. `rust-toolchain.toml` `channel` a dated `nightly-YYYY-MM-DD`;
37. `rust-toolchain.toml` `channel = "beta"`; 38. `rust-toolchain.toml`
`channel` unclassifiable as either a version literal or a known track;
39. `rust-toolchain.toml` with `path`;
40. **disposition precedence** — `rust-toolchain.toml` carrying both `path` and
`channel = "nightly"`, reported `build_toolchain_package_influence_forbidden`
and not `build_toolchain_metadata_mismatch`;
41. manifest carrying an executable path, URL, channel, track, install command,
or environment override; 42. descriptor target carrying any of the same;
43. toolchain tree changed between Stage A and fingerprinting;
44. external command failing Stage A with no acquisition performed;
45. **fail-fast before lookup** — the current resolved toolchain fails Stage A,
so the operation fails there with no cache lookup, no candidate consulted, no
rebuild, and no mutation; 46. dry-run reporting `blocked` rather than
`unsupported`.

Guidance catalog:

47. every one of the twelve reasons resolves to an active entry for every
    supported toolchain and platform;
48. a catalog missing one reason for one supported toolchain fails the release
    gate;
49. two active entries for one `(toolchain_id, reason, platform)` tuple fail the
    gate;
50. `superseded_by` naming a lower, equal, or non-existent revision fails the
    gate;
51. `superseded_by` naming a different tuple fails the gate;
52. a superseded entry stays resolvable while selection returns the active
    revision;
53. each of the twelve codes emits a `guidance_id` whose revision component is
    present and whose entry is active.

Identity guards:

54. `curator-go-toolchain-v1` bytes unchanged; 55. rc.4 byte-frozen digests
unchanged; 56. a requirement change alone producing an identical cache key;
57. a `compatibility`-set change alone producing an identical cache key;
58. a catalog `primary_source` or revision change alone producing an identical
cache key.

